Before editing, read `.agents/docs/systems/client-data.md` (what belongs on the client, the server,
or both; MPQ load order; extractor limits; `*_dbc` overlays). For any change that ships an MPQ or
server `data/` files follow `.agents/skills/build-client-patch/SKILL.md`; OS-specific commands are
in its `reference-windows-linux.md`.

Hard rules from those docs:

- Custom world files go in `Data/patch-4.MPQ`, DBCs in `Data/enUS/patch-enUS-4.MPQ`. Never past
  `patch-5`, never lettered patches. Archives are MPQ v2.
- A DBC changed on one side must change on the other in the same release.
- Binaries never enter git; only `client-patches/manifest.json` does.
